    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling production of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), whose matchup against Ober is our most promising opportunity. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from Ober\u2019s slow delivery, which boosts his base expectation, and his placement in the leadoff spot maximizes his counting stat potential. Alongside him, **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) stand out as elite starts. **Luis Robert Jr.** gains a sharp platoon advantage against the lefty P\u00e9rez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a high floor due to favorable park factors and the ability to drive in runs from the heart of the order against Sandoval. **Jacob Wilson** (70.33) also remains a core play, as his plate discipline and favorable spot against Martinez yield a high efficiency score that keeps him firmly in our starting nine.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just shy of our 50.0 threshold with a 46.31 score. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the speed we desperately crave, the combination of a tough outing against Imanaga and a suboptimal spot in the batting order pushed him to the bench in favor of more stable output. We are closely monitoring the 31% rain risk surrounding the game involving **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**; if that game is delayed or postponed, we lose two starters who rely on aggressive base-running against the pitcher's delivery pace. Additionally, while **Kyle Tucker** (71.17) and **Andy Pages** (65.78) are strong, their scores are contingent on confirmed lineups against Wacha. Owners should ensure no last-minute shifts occur for **Liam Hicks** or these outfielders, as the current projections assume standard placement for our projected lineup.",
